  "slug": "ambarella-physical-ai-workload-integration",
  "title": "VLA, SLAM and navigation on one SoC: the questions are just beginning",
  "deck": "Ambarella has put SmolVLA, SLAM and navigation on the N1-655. The more useful question now is whether these tasks can keep working together, reliably and over time.",
  "summary": "Putting several robotics workloads on one chip opens integration possibilities while leaving resource-sharing and sustained-operation questions. From the N1-655 demo to the X7’s incremental acceleration approach, this essay asks how a platform capability becomes something a customer can ship.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": null,
